  <reporting-org ref="US-GOV-1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">U.S. Agency for International Development</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Bangsamoro  Autonomous Region in Muslim Mindanao (BARMM) Health Capacity Building (BARMMHealth)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Philippines):  .Operating within a complex political, security, and social environment, USAID, through the BARMMHealth activity, will work with the BARMM Ministry of Health, Commission on Population, and other key partners to respond to unmet need for voluntary modern family planning (FP) services and high teenage pregnancy rates. Family Planning-earmarked funds will support the following key interventions: .Increase the correct use of lactational amenorrhea method (LAM) and the transition to other modern FP methods by developing and implementing a LAM Tracking Tool; developing an educational job aid for community health workers; designing and disseminating an educational packet for community influencers; and training company nurses to provide support to breastfeeding mothers.Promote convergence of comprehensive sexuality education and adolescent reproductive health by designing and implementing social and behavior change communication approaches to help adolescents build life skills; ensuring functionality of adolescent friendly health facilities; and providing adolescents access to a continuum of reproductive health care.Model sustainable health financing in the Universal Health Care integration sites of Basilan and Maguindanao provinces by assisting them in establishing province-wide health boards; integrating health services through a province-wide Health Care Provider Network, pooling resources at the provincial level; and utilizing health investments efficiently through a functional Social Health Fund. Increase the capacity of healthcare providers to implement the Field Health Services Information System for FP indicators and ensure a systematic approach to data integrity and reliability for effective planning, budgeting, and decision-making.Strengthen implementation of continuous quality improvement in pilot cities/municipalities and institutionalize the practice at the regional level to improve overall service utilization and client satisfaction. . .</narrative>
  </description>
